    "title": "<p>Diagnostic criteria for myelodysplastic/myeloproliferative neoplasm with neutrophilia (MDS/MPN-N)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Eric Solary",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"background: #daeef3; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Essential:</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Peripheral blood white blood cell count &ge;&nbsp;13&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/L, with neutrophilia and &ge;&nbsp;10% circulating immature myeloid cells (promyelocytes, myelocytes, and metamyelocytes), as well as neutrophilic dysplasia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hypercellular bone marrow with granulocytic predominance and granulocytic dysplasia, with or without dysplasia in the megakaryocytic and erythroid lineages</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&lt;&nbsp;20% blasts in blood and bone marrow</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not meeting diagnostic criteria for myeloproliferative neoplasms (specifically, exclusion of <em>BCR</em>::<em>ABL1</em> fusion)<sup>a</sup>, myeloid/lymphoid neoplasms with eosinophilia and tyrosine kinase gene fusions, chronic myelomonocytic leukaemia, or myelodysplastic/myeloproliferative neoplasm with <em>SF3B1 </em>mutation and thrombocytosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Desirable:</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Detection of <em>SETBP1 </em>and/or <em>ETNK1 </em>mutations</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Absence of mutations in <em>JAK2</em>, <em>CALR</em>, <em>MPL</em>, and <em>CSF3R</em><sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">The</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"> diagnosis of MDS/MPN-N requires exclusion of <em>BCR</em>::<em>ABL1</em> fusion, which requires careful evaluation to exclude cryptic rearrangements and/or alternate <em>BCR</em>::<em>ABL1</em> transcripts by available methodologies (e.g. cytogenetics, in&nbsp;situ hybridization, or PCR-based assays). <sup>b</sup>Mutations in these genes are uncommon in MDS/MPN-N and should prompt morphological review to exclude alternative diagnoses.</span></p>",
